PUPPET WORKSHOP -- STANDING NOTICE CONCERNING SASORI OF THE RED SAND
Kazekage Office and Puppet Brigade. Read by all Brigade members.

Sasori, grandson of the honored elder Chiyo, was once the greatest puppeteer
Sunagakure ever produced -- and became its most notorious traitor. He defected,
took the name Sasori of the Red Sand for the blood he shed, and joined the
Akatsuki. This notice records what the Brigade must never forget.

Points of standing record:
- Sasori pioneered forbidden human puppetry, converting slain foes -- and his own
  body -- into puppets. He is known to have abducted and made a puppet of the
  Third Kazekage, stealing the iron-sand techniques thereby.
- His "collection" numbered many human puppets, granting him a hundred hostile
  bodies to command at once.
- He was slain in the operation to rescue Lord Gaara, defeated in a duel of
  puppet masters by his own grandmother Chiyo.

Any recovered Sasori-pattern puppet or poison is contraband, delivered
immediately to the Kazekage Office. His arts are cautionary, not aspirational.
Filed under Brigade seal.
